CodeAtlas is an independent, Rust-native implementation of codebase architecture
analysis. Its design — the analysis.json output schema, the component/relation
model, and the overall feature set — is informed by the open-source project
CodeBoarding (https://github.com/CodeBoarding/CodeBoarding), released under the
MIT License (Copyright (c) 2025 CodeBoarding).

No upstream source code or documentation prose is copied into CodeAtlas; the
interfaces and data-model shapes are reproduced for output-format compatibility.
